ordCount, and the final GET response records do not contain the previously recorded affected sample records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /sample-data/reset without required confirmation, reads GET /sample-data, then repeats the reset with explicit confirmation and reads GET /sample-data again.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and sample records exist; the client records the GET /sample-data response records and recordCount before attempting replacement.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The unconfirmed response status is the contract-declared 422 or 409 and the intervening GET response records and recordCount are unchanged; the confirmed response reports the completed replacement status and resulting recordCount, and the final GET response records contain the replacement sample records rather than the previously recorded affected sample records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /sample-data/replace without required confirmation, reads GET /sample-data, then repeats replacement with explicit confirmation and reads GET /sample-data again.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, loads, resets, or replaces sample records, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined sample status and records, avoid duplicate loading, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is configured with an App PostgreSQL connection and a client successfully creates or updates a contract resource.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the saved value and the returned record has the same id and field values as the successful write response.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process res